      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It takes a lot of courage to admit feeling this way. It's essential to recognize that your perceived weight and responsibility may not be entirely your fault. Many children carry stress and weighty responsibilities themselves, and it's okay to acknowledge that you're doing your best as a parent. Consider having an open and honest conversation with your kids about how you're feeling, as this can help to release some of the guilt and burden you're carrying.",
